      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1903-12-24_WidnesExaminer_art0025" n="art0025">
        <head>AN HUMBLE HERO.</head>
        <p>AN HUMBLE HERO.</p>
        <p>A well-known figure, familiar to every City man is the little wiry hawker of penny goode at the corner of the Bank, looking down Moorgate Street, which beat he has worked for twenty-eight years, ever since an accident deprived him of his left leg. Walker is hit name, and his , inner life holds For</p>
        <p>quite a quiet</p>
        <p>_ ----, ' \ `\'r '' -.k oivi, '' ; k 4,4 - ''',), XX /</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1903-12-24_WidnesExaminer_art0026" n="art0026">
        <head>romance</head>
        <p>romance</p>
        <p>years, in addi- tion to keeping up a home by hawking, his object in life has</p>
        <p>been not only</p>
        <p>to improve him-</p>
        <p>self bit to help</p>
        <p>others; and many a poor</p>
        <p>cripple,. a .Class</p>
        <p>wicii which he</p>
        <p>has peculiar</p>
        <p>sympathy, has</p>
        <p>to be</p>
